CSS BACKGROUND SHORTHAND PROPERTY
================================

👉 Definition:
The background shorthand property is used to set multiple background properties in a single line,
reducing code and improving readability.


WHY USE SHORTHAND?
==================

👉 Problem:
Writing many background properties separately increases code length.

👉 Solution:
Use shorthand to combine them into one clean declaration.


LONGHAND VS SHORTHAND
====================

👉 Longhand (multiple lines):

.box {
    background-color: #eee;
    background-image: url("img.jpg");
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-position: center;
    background-size: cover;
}

⬇️ Converts to ⬇️

👉 Shorthand (single line):

.box {
    background: #eee url("img.jpg") no-repeat center / cover;
}


BASIC SHORTHAND STRUCTURE
========================

👉 General pattern:
background: color image repeat position / size attachment origin clip;


IMPORTANT ORDER RULE ⚠️
=======================

👉 Order is flexible EXCEPT for one rule:

➡️ background-size MUST come AFTER background-position  
➡️ background-size MUST be separated using a slash (/)

✔️ Correct:
background: center / cover;

❌ Wrong:
background: cover center;


MOST COMMON REAL-WORLD USAGE
============================

👉 Used in hero sections, banners, cards:

.box {
    background: url("img.jpg") no-repeat center / cover;
}


PROPERTY BREAKDOWN (MENTAL MAP)
===============================

color        ➜ background-color  
url()        ➜ background-image  
no-repeat    ➜ background-repeat  
center       ➜ background-position  
/ cover      ➜ background-size  


BACKGROUND-SIZE SPECIAL RULE 🚨
===============================

👉 background-size CANNOT exist alone in shorthand.

➡️ It MUST follow background-position  
➡️ It MUST use a slash (/)

Example:
center / contain


MULTIPLE BACKGROUND IMAGES
=========================

👉 You can layer backgrounds.

➡️ Each layer is separated by a comma  
➡️ First image appears on TOP

.box {
    background:
        url("top.png") no-repeat center / contain,
        url("bottom.jpg") repeat left top;
}


DEFAULT VALUES (IF YOU SKIP THEM)
================================

👉 Browser automatically fills missing values:

background-color     ➜ transparent  
background-repeat    ➜ repeat  
background-position  ➜ 0% 0%  
background-size      ➜ auto  
background-attachment➜ scroll  


CLEARING BACKGROUND 🧹
=====================

👉 Removes ALL background-related properties:

.box {
    background: none;
}


COMMON MISTAKES ⚠️
==================

❌ Forgetting the slash for background-size  
❌ Writing background-size before background-position  
❌ Assuming shorthand order is fully fixed  
❌ Forgetting to give height to the element  


BEST PRACTICE ✅
================

👉 While learning:
Use individual background properties.

👉 In production:
Use shorthand for cleaner and shorter code.


INTERVIEW WORDING 🎤
===================

👉 “The background shorthand property allows multiple background-related properties
 such as image, position, size, repeat, and color to be defined in a single CSS declaration.”
